#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:223
msgid "Poll Rate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:225
msgid "``Path: GTM > Mouse > Poll Rate``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:227
msgid ""
"The polling rate (poll rate) is the frequency at which data from the "
"CharaChorder's mouse functionality is sent to the device it's connected "
"to. In other words, how often it updates the cursor's position to the "
"computer. This is typically expressed in Hz (Hertz), with the average "
"gaming mouse reporting data at 1000 Hz, which means 1000 times every "
"second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:229
msgid ""
"However, :doc:`CCOS<CCOS>` uses ms (milliseconds) which is directly "
"inverse to Hz. 1 ms is equal to 1000 Hz, 2 ms is equal to 500 Hz, and "
"1000 ms is equal to 1 Hz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst
msgid "An Explanation of Hz to ms conversion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:233
msgid ""
"In the context of frequency and period (time duration), the relationship "
"is inverse. Frequency is the number of cycles per second, measured in Hz."
" The period is the time it takes for one cycle to complete, measured in "
"seconds (s). The formula is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:235
msgid "``Frequency (Hz) = 1/Period (s), where s = 1000 ms``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../GenerativeTextMenu.rst:237
msgid ""
"If you convert the period to milliseconds (ms), the relationship remains "
"inverse. For instance, if you have a frequency of 1000 Hz, the period is "
"1 ms (because 1 second = 1000 milliseconds). As the frequency increases, "
"the period (measured in ms) decreases."
msgstr ""

